<BaseLayout title="About & editorial policy" description="How Signal & Field researches, writes, sources, and updates its articles.">
  <header class="page-top"><div class="article-shell"><div class="section-kicker">About this publication</div><h1>Useful first.<br />Accurate always.</h1><p>Signal & Field is an independent technology blog covering AI, cars, and smart farming.</p></div></header>
  <div class="article-body article-shell">
    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <p>Every article starts with a concrete reader question. We favor official documentation, original research, public data, and firsthand observations. We link to sources near the claims they support and date substantial updates.</p>
    <p>Automated tools may help with research, drafting, and formatting. A human review is required before publication. We do not publish unsupported factual claims or present generated material as firsthand testing.</p>
    <h2>Corrections and commercial content</h2>
    <p>Corrections should be reflected in the article and its updated date. If advertising, affiliate links, or sponsorships are introduced, they will be labeled clearly and kept separate from editorial judgments.</p>
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>Articles explain technologies and tradeoffs. They are informational and should be checked against current primary sources before making important purchasing, safety, or operational decisions.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
